[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186134132 :question/answer-fields 17592186130948] {:db/id 17592186133926 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-598960e7-33b5-506e-acd3-0cfad9c377b7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-598960e7-33b5-506e-acd3-0cfad9c377b7" :question/id #uuid "598960e7-33b5-506e-acd3-0cfad9c377b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162231" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=x\\,i-z\\,j+y\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=2\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t).\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i-z\\,j+y\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(2\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k)\\cdot (-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))\\cdot (-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\cdot \\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t) \\\\  & =\\pi {sin}^{2}⁡(\\pi t)+\\pi {cos}^{2}⁡(\\pi t) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\pi \\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\pi [t]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi (2-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5ff271c5-90b5-5fb1-aa9a-8de6b8aed244"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5ff271c5-90b5-5fb1-aa9a-8de6b8aed244" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ff271c5-90b5-5fb1-aa9a-8de6b8aed244" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-81f383ab-ca0f-54cf-8cd9-153255df4842" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4543906-53e0-543b-8b49-5cef8732311e" "answer-82168b66-7a44-5eb9-8fa3-a04f1522bfc1" "answer-77c7dfa0-202b-5af6-9228-dc6355dcb12c" "answer-81f383ab-ca0f-54cf-8cd9-153255df4842" "answer-ac321221-fe9b-5704-a522-fd0ed1517250"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4543906-53e0-543b-8b49-5cef8732311e" :answer/id #uuid "c4543906-53e0-543b-8b49-5cef8732311e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82168b66-7a44-5eb9-8fa3-a04f1522bfc1" :answer/id #uuid "82168b66-7a44-5eb9-8fa3-a04f1522bfc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77c7dfa0-202b-5af6-9228-dc6355dcb12c" :answer/id #uuid "77c7dfa0-202b-5af6-9228-dc6355dcb12c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81f383ab-ca0f-54cf-8cd9-153255df4842" :answer/id #uuid "81f383ab-ca0f-54cf-8cd9-153255df4842" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac321221-fe9b-5704-a522-fd0ed1517250" :answer/id #uuid "ac321221-fe9b-5704-a522-fd0ed1517250" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134133 :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=(y-x)\\,i$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+({t}^{3}-t)\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}-t,\\,y={t}^{3}-t,\\,z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t).\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(y-x)\\,i \\\\  & =({t}^{3}-t-{t}^{2}+t)\\,i \\\\  & =({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,)\\,k \\\\  & =(2t-1)\\,i+(3{t}^{2}-1)\\,j+2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\,({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})\\,i\\,)\\cdot (\\,(2t-1)\\,i+(3{t}^{2}-1)\\,j+2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k\\,) \\\\  & =({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})\\cdot (2t-1)+0\\cdot (3{t}^{2}-1)+0\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t) \\\\  & =2{t}^{4}-{t}^{3}-2{t}^{3}+{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{4}-3{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\,2{t}^{4}-3{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}\\,)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{t}^{5}}{5}-\\frac{3{t}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{3})-(0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{60}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186130954 :answer-field/correct 17592186130955 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-598960e7-33b5-506e-acd3-0cfad9c377b7" :question/id #uuid "598960e7-33b5-506e-acd3-0cfad9c377b7"] ["question-598960e7-33b5-506e-acd3-0cfad9c377b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162231"] ["question-598960e7-33b5-506e-acd3-0cfad9c377b7" :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=x\\,i-z\\,j+y\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=2\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2).$"] ["question-598960e7-33b5-506e-acd3-0cfad9c377b7" :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t).\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i-z\\,j+y\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(2\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k)\\cdot (-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\,j+\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))\\cdot (-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)\\cdot \\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t) \\\\  & =\\pi {sin}^{2}⁡(\\pi t)+\\pi {cos}^{2}⁡(\\pi t) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\pi \\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\pi [t]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi (2-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-598960e7-33b5-506e-acd3-0cfad9c377b7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-5ff271c5-90b5-5fb1-aa9a-8de6b8aed244" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ff271c5-90b5-5fb1-aa9a-8de6b8aed244"] ["answer-c4543906-53e0-543b-8b49-5cef8732311e" :answer/id #uuid "c4543906-53e0-543b-8b49-5cef8732311e"] ["answer-c4543906-53e0-543b-8b49-5cef8732311e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c4543906-53e0-543b-8b49-5cef8732311e" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-82168b66-7a44-5eb9-8fa3-a04f1522bfc1" :answer/id #uuid "82168b66-7a44-5eb9-8fa3-a04f1522bfc1"] ["answer-82168b66-7a44-5eb9-8fa3-a04f1522bfc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-82168b66-7a44-5eb9-8fa3-a04f1522bfc1" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-77c7dfa0-202b-5af6-9228-dc6355dcb12c" :answer/id #uuid "77c7dfa0-202b-5af6-9228-dc6355dcb12c"] ["answer-77c7dfa0-202b-5af6-9228-dc6355dcb12c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-77c7dfa0-202b-5af6-9228-dc6355dcb12c" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-81f383ab-ca0f-54cf-8cd9-153255df4842" :answer/id #uuid "81f383ab-ca0f-54cf-8cd9-153255df4842"] ["answer-81f383ab-ca0f-54cf-8cd9-153255df4842" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-81f383ab-ca0f-54cf-8cd9-153255df4842" :answer/value "2\\pi "] ["answer-ac321221-fe9b-5704-a522-fd0ed1517250" :answer/id #uuid "ac321221-fe9b-5704-a522-fd0ed1517250"] ["answer-ac321221-fe9b-5704-a522-fd0ed1517250" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ac321221-fe9b-5704-a522-fd0ed1517250" :answer/value "\\pi "] ["answer-field-5ff271c5-90b5-5fb1-aa9a-8de6b8aed244" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-5ff271c5-90b5-5fb1-aa9a-8de6b8aed244" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-5ff271c5-90b5-5fb1-aa9a-8de6b8aed244" :answer-field/correct "answer-81f383ab-ca0f-54cf-8cd9-153255df4842"] ["answer-field-5ff271c5-90b5-5fb1-aa9a-8de6b8aed244" :