i \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t)\\,k\\,) \\\\  & =({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})\\cdot (2t-1)+0\\cdot (3{t}^{2}-1)+0\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi t) \\\\  & =2{t}^{4}-{t}^{3}-2{t}^{3}+{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{4}-3{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\,2{t}^{4}-3{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}\\,)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{t}^{5}}{5}-\\frac{3{t}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{3})-(0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{60}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186134133 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186130954 :answer-field/correct 17592186130955]] "retractions" [[17592186134133 :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x, y, z) = (y - x)i$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t) = (t^{2} - t)i + (t^{3} - t)j + \\sin (2πt)k$ for $t ∈ [0, 1)$."] [17592186134132 :question/answer-fields 17592186130948]]}]